# Smart-X (Parts 1–3) - manual API tests (Visual Studio / VS Code REST Client / Rider)
@api = http://localhost:5261
@pumpA = 24:6F:28:C3:00:20
@moistureB = 24:6F:28:A1:00:02
@meterMain = 24:6F:28:B2:00:10

### Health
GET {{api}}/api/health

### 1. Dictionary O(1) lookup by MAC
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices/{{moistureB}}

### 2. Search / filter (category index + alert state). log=true teaches the predictive engine
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?category=Actuator
###
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?state=alerting
###
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?q=pump&log=true

### 3. Device uplink -> standard Queue (normal reading)
POST {{api}}/api/stream/ingest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "{{moistureB}}", "value": 41.5 }

### 4. Device uplink -> PriorityQueue (critical moisture drop bypasses the queue)
POST {{api}}/api/stream/ingest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "{{moistureB}}", "value": 9.0 }

### 5. Power surge on the main meter -> PriorityQueue
POST {{api}}/api/stream/ingest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "{{meterMain}}", "value": 4600 }

### 6. Flood 600 routine packets THEN one critical packet - critical is processed first
POST {{api}}/api/stream/simulate/burst
Content-Type: application/json

{ "standardCount": 600, "includeCritical": true, "criticalMac": "{{moistureB}}" }

### 7. Inject one critical reading for a device
POST {{api}}/api/stream/simulate/critical/{{moistureB}}

### 8. Inspect processed order, lanes and latency
GET {{api}}/api/stream/snapshot

### 9. Queue and alert statistics only
GET {{api}}/api/stream/stats

### 10. Manual override -> pushed onto the undo Stack
POST {{api}}/api/stream/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "{{pumpA}}", "action": "ON" }

### 11. Bulk override: shut down all valves (ONE stack entry)
POST {{api}}/api/stream/commands/bulk
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "OFF", "nameContains": "Valve", "label": "Shut down all valves" }

### 12. Undo (Stack.Pop) / Redo
POST {{api}}/api/stream/commands/undo
###
POST {{api}}/api/stream/commands/redo

### 13. Command history
GET {{api}}/api/stream/commands

### 14. Device downlink: Pump A collects its pending commands
GET {{api}}/api/stream/outbox/{{pumpA}}

### 15. SortedDictionary timeline (time-ordered)
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices/{{moistureB}}/timeline?minutes=5

### 16. Alerts (HashSet) and alert history
GET {{api}}/api/stream/alerts
###
GET {{api}}/api/stream/alerts/history

### 17. Predictive engine
GET {{api}}/api/stream/suggestions
###
GET {{api}}/api/stream/patterns

### ================= Final PoE: Network Topology & Mesh Routing =================

### Whole mesh: nodes, links, MST flags, articulation points, events
GET {{api}}/api/topology

### Route tracking by MAC: MST route + cheapest path (Dijkstra) + backup hop
GET {{api}}/api/topology/route/24:6F:28:A1:00:02

### BFS from the gateway: every connected device, and every device that is down
GET {{api}}/api/topology/bfs

### DFS limited to the Zone 1 subnet
GET {{api}}/api/topology/dfs?zone=Zone%201

### Minimum spanning tree — Prim's (binary heap)
GET {{api}}/api/topology/mst?algorithm=prim

### Minimum spanning tree — Kruskal's (sorted edges + union–find)
GET {{api}}/api/topology/mst?algorithm=kruskal

### Simulate a relay failure (run again to restore it)
POST {{api}}/api/topology/nodes/24:6F:28:B2:00:10/toggle

### Simulate a broken radio link (run again to restore it)
POST {{api}}/api/topology/links/toggle
Content-Type: application/json

{ "a": "24:6F:28:00:00:00", "b": "24:6F:28:C3:00:23" }

### Clear every simulated failure
POST {{api}}/api/topology/reset

### What an ESP32 reports: its neighbours' signal strength (weak signal → link cost rises)
POST {{api}}/api/topology/neighbors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "24:6F:28:C3:00:20", "neighbors": [ { "neighborMac": "24:6F:28:B2:00:11", "rssi": -90 } ] }

### AVL history: Moisture Sensor A between 14:00 and 16:00 (SAST) yesterday — change the date
GET {{api}}/api/topology/history/24:6F:28:A1:00:01?from=2026-10-21T14:00:00%2B02:00&to=2026-10-21T16:00:00%2B02:00

### AVL history: last 6 hours
GET {{api}}/api/topology/history/24:6F:28:A1:00:01?minutes=360

### Size and height of every sensor's AVL tree
GET {{api}}/api/topology/history

### Scale benchmark: AVL vs linear scan, graph algorithms on a 2 000-node mesh
GET {{api}}/api/topology/benchmark?nodes=2000
